# TriviaBot Answer and Clue Cleaning

## Rule: separate cleaning for clues vs answers

- **Clues**: Use `cleanClueText()` (or equivalent) to strip player responses, host asides, and artifacts. This can be aggressive.
- **Answers**: Use a **gentler** `cleanAnswerText()` (or equivalent) so full answer text is preserved. Do **not** use the same aggressive clue cleaner for answers.

## Why

- Using clue-style cleaning on answers led to truncated answers (e.g. only "the" or "The"). Answers should keep the full response text while only removing obvious artifacts (e.g. parenthetical asides, [Laughter], "Triple Stumper").

## When editing scrapers or parsers

- Any script that extracts both clues and answers should call separate cleaners. Preserve trailing words and normal phrasing in answers; only remove clear non-answer artifacts.
